-- Scans +\ *\ max\ along index-order views: one running value per selected cell (ex16). Twin of 16-scans.bqn.
-- Header lines 1 and 3 spell generated views (↕steps |> route A B; Eye + ↕n * fwd); the .bqn fixture realizes both as the masks route/ray, whose declared order is index order, so the twin scans over those mask scopes; line 2 is verbatim.
-- The out vector lengths (5, 4, 5) pin the same-length invariant: result length = popcount of the mask, never world length; unselected multiplier/height cells are decoy 9s, so any 9 in a product or max is a selection leak.
--! registry 16-scans

--! out 3 4 8 10 15
+\ Weight @ Route

--! out 2 6 9 18
*\ Multiplier @ comboChain

--! out 3 3 4 4 5
max\ Height @ Ray
